  "notes": "Verb type: {一段動詞|いちだんどうし} (ichidan verb)\nTransitivity: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\nPair: {煮詰|につ}まる (intransitive)\n\nSENSE 1 (COOKING):\n- Reduces liquid by evaporation\n- Concentrates flavors\n\nSENSE 2 (FIGURATIVE):\n- Used for discussions, plans, projects\n- Means to work out details thoroughly\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ソースを{煮詰|につ}める: to reduce sauce\n- {議論|ぎろん}を{煮詰|につ}める: to thrash out a discussion\n- {企画|きかく}を{煮詰|につ}める: to finalize a plan\n\nNOTE ON {煮詰|につ}まる:\nThe intransitive {煮詰|につ}まる has developed a negative meaning \"to reach a stalemate\" (discussions boiling dry), though traditionally it meant \"to be finalized.\"",
